1
00:00:05,505 --> 00:00:06,631
Hands in the air!
Don't turn around!

2
00:00:06,756 --> 00:00:07,798
- Okay.
- Don't turn around!

3
00:00:07,924 --> 00:00:08,966
Get on the ground!

4
00:00:09,091 --> 00:00:10,510
- Hurry up!
- Give me your gun!

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:11,928
I said do it!

6
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,182
Your 2-11 pager. Now!

7
00:00:16,641 --> 00:00:17,767
Put it down!

8
00:00:21,938 --> 00:00:23,564
Get outta here! Go!

9
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:33,032
The driver's calling it in!
Turn it up!

10
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:36,160
Come on! Let's hurry up!

11
00:00:37,119 --> 00:00:38,162
Go!

12
00:00:40,748 --> 00:00:41,791
Let's go.

13
00:00:45,711 --> 00:00:46,921
Come on! Come on!

14
00:00:54,512 --> 00:00:56,347
It's this little cabin
in the hill country...

15
00:00:56,472 --> 00:00:58,683
rustic, charming, very romantic.

16
00:00:58,808 --> 00:01:01,519
- Rustic as in no running water or...
- Well, would that be a problem?

17
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:03,145
Well, when you said,
"Let's go away for the weekend"

18
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:06,357
I was kinda hoping for the kind of place
that leaves a mint on the pillow.

19
00:01:07,108 --> 00:01:08,442
- Hey, Cho.
- Hey.

20
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:10,820
We have three men robbing
an armored truck.

21
00:01:11,070 --> 00:01:12,697
They subdued the guard,
unloaded the cash

22
00:01:12,822 --> 00:01:13,906
got out in 60 seconds.

23
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:15,700
Land speed record. Any witnesses?

24
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:17,201
They gave us approximate
heights and weights

25
00:01:17,326 --> 00:01:18,494
but nothing groundbreaking.

26
00:01:18,911 --> 00:01:20,538
Tactics match a team
that's been knocking off

27
00:01:20,663 --> 00:01:21,956
payday loan shops around town.

28
00:01:22,456 --> 00:01:23,583
But those were two-man jobs.

29
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:25,626
Well, it sounds like they made
a new friend.

30
00:01:25,793 --> 00:01:28,921
Bank manager says this is the biggest
cash delivery of the year.

31
00:01:29,213 --> 00:01:31,716
$600,000 in wrapped bricks.

32
00:01:31,841 --> 00:01:33,551
Any tracking devices or dye packs?

33
00:01:33,843 --> 00:01:35,845
They add those after the cash
is broken down.

34
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:39,181
- Lucky robbers.
- Luck is the planning you don't see.

35
00:01:39,348 --> 00:01:40,391
What kinda planning?

36
00:01:40,516 --> 00:01:41,684
You think someone with the bank
is involved.

37
00:01:41,809 --> 00:01:44,687
Seems likely. A score this big
literally gift-wrapped?

38
00:01:45,062 --> 00:01:46,772
All right, we'll get surveillance up
on the bank employees.

39
00:01:46,897 --> 00:01:49,150
Well, that sounds like a hassle.
Let's just ask 'em.

40
00:01:50,693 --> 00:01:52,903
Pull footage from the surveillance cameras
in the area.

41
00:01:55,656 --> 00:01:57,700
Good morning. Can I have
everyone's attention, please?

42
00:01:58,367 --> 00:01:59,910
Thank you. Uh, quick question...

43
00:02:00,119 --> 00:02:02,872
which one of you was the accomplice
to the robbery this morning?

44
00:02:03,205 --> 00:02:04,332
Sorry. Who are you?

45
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:06,459
Patrick Jane, FBI.
You?

46
00:02:06,709 --> 00:02:10,046
Gil Clark. I'm the branch manager.
Did you just accuse my people?

47
00:02:10,171 --> 00:02:12,506
Gil, I did. Agent Cho will explain.

48
00:02:12,882 --> 00:02:14,550
Hi. How you doing?
Nice to meet you.

49
00:02:14,675 --> 00:02:15,801
Sorry to hear about the robbery.

50
00:02:15,926 --> 00:02:18,179
- So, what the hell is going on here?
- Just be patient, sir.

51
00:02:18,304 --> 00:02:20,264
- Sorry to hear about the robbery.
- I mean, this is outrageous.

52
00:02:20,389 --> 00:02:22,350
No. Not really. Not yet.

53
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:26,228
And thank you.
Well, that was my pleasure.

54
00:02:26,354 --> 00:02:28,814
Uh, let me tell you something
about guilt.

55
00:02:29,023 --> 00:02:32,193
It's physical...
increased perspiration, racing heart.

56
00:02:32,652 --> 00:02:33,944
But when I just shook your hands

57
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:37,239
most of you were relatively
calm and relaxed

58
00:02:37,365 --> 00:02:39,200
which is incredible
given the circumstances.

59
00:02:39,450 --> 00:02:42,912
Except for, uh, you,
Ken Fletcher, senior teller.

60
00:02:43,162 --> 00:02:45,581
Your heart, my friend,
is racing like a greyhound.

61
00:02:45,831 --> 00:02:47,083
What is that supposed to mean?

62
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:49,168
And your left hand
keeps touching your pocket.

63
00:02:49,293 --> 00:02:50,544
What do you got in there?

64
00:02:51,253 --> 00:02:52,797
- Empty it.
- It...

65
00:02:52,922 --> 00:02:53,964
Now.

66
00:02:58,052 --> 00:02:59,345
Looks like a burner.

67
00:03:00,054 --> 00:03:01,555
Phone you don't wanna be traced.

68
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:03,391
Who gave this to you, sir?

69
00:03:03,766 --> 00:03:05,976
- I-I-I don't know. I mean, I-I...
- Answer the question.

70
00:03:06,102 --> 00:03:08,646
- Who gave this to you, sir?
- I don't, I-I-I just, I-I...

71
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:11,774
Oh, no. I think you killed him.

72
00:03:25,093 --> 00:03:26,970
Fainting isn't evidence of anything.

73
00:03:27,638 --> 00:03:28,931
I'm hypoglycemic.

74
00:03:29,139 --> 00:03:31,683
I didn't have breakfast.
My blood sugar was in the basement.

75
00:03:31,892 --> 00:03:34,978
So you got the burner phone
because of your blood sugar?

76
00:03:36,396 --> 00:03:38,607
You doubled the cash order
at the bank this week.

77
00:03:39,233 --> 00:03:40,651
Was that the blood sugar talking?

78
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:44,530
My client is not answering
questions at this time.

79
00:03:44,780 --> 00:03:47,199
I don't think Ken here,
with his health issues

80
00:03:47,574 --> 00:03:48,867
is really up for prison.

81
00:03:50,118 --> 00:03:51,829
So let's improve his outlook.

82
00:03:52,496 --> 00:03:54,206
Start with the robbers' names.

83
00:03:56,041 --> 00:03:57,084
What robbers?

84
00:03:57,626 --> 00:03:59,127
I don't see any robbers.

85
00:04:00,003 --> 00:04:01,797
Call me when you have somebody
in custody.

86
00:04:12,599 --> 00:04:13,642
{\an8}He's holding out.

87
00:04:14,142 --> 00:04:15,936
{\an8}He won't talk until we have the others.

88
00:04:16,061 --> 00:04:17,437
Maybe we can track 'em down
with his phone.

89
00:04:17,646 --> 00:04:18,689
{\an8}Yeah, try it.

90
00:04:19,690 --> 00:04:20,941
{\an8}Know what? You run this one.

91
00:04:21,275 --> 00:04:23,151
Might as well.
You'll be in charge soon enough.

92
00:04:23,443 --> 00:04:25,028
- You sure?
- Yeah.

93
00:04:25,404 --> 00:04:26,864
They're tired of hearing
my voice anyway.

94
00:04:26,989 --> 00:04:28,031
{\an8}All right.

95
00:04:29,408 --> 00:04:31,493
{\an8}"So, my friend has
this League of Legends team"

96
00:04:31,618 --> 00:04:34,162
{\an8}and they're playing a tournament
in Houston on Saturday.

97
00:04:34,288 --> 00:04:36,206
{\an8}I crush League of Legends.

98
00:04:36,707 --> 00:04:38,750
- You wanna go?
- That'd be awesome.

99
00:04:39,042 --> 00:04:40,377
{\an8}I figure we could drive down

100
00:04:40,502 --> 00:04:42,421
{\an8}and then maybe afterward
we could stick around

101
00:04:42,546 --> 00:04:43,714
and have dinner.

102
00:04:44,089 --> 00:04:45,799
- Yeah.
- Really?

103
00:04:46,174 --> 00:04:48,010
{\an8}Sure. Let's do it.

104
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:50,470
{\an8}Cool. Yeah. I'll let him know.

105
00:04:50,804 --> 00:04:51,847
{\an8}Hey.

106
00:04:52,723 --> 00:04:53,891
{\an8}Have you guys seen Jane and Lisbon?

107
00:04:54,057 --> 00:04:56,059
Lisbon went to get the rest
of the security video.

108
00:04:56,268 --> 00:04:58,312
Jane just said he was running
an errand.

109
00:04:58,687 --> 00:05:00,272
Austin PD found the getaway car

110
00:05:00,397 --> 00:05:02,608
about a half-mile from the bank,
no prints.

111
00:05:02,733 --> 00:05:04,192
{\an8}Tell them to dust it again just to be sure.

112
00:05:04,568 --> 00:05:05,611
{\an8}Anything off the phone?

113
00:05:05,736 --> 00:05:07,404
Fletcher made about a dozen calls
this week

114
00:05:07,529 --> 00:05:09,406
to another burner...
no way to tell who has that one.

115
00:05:09,531 --> 00:05:10,574
All right.

116
00:05:12,868 --> 00:05:14,870
{\an8}He must have been calling the robbers.

117
00:05:14,995 --> 00:05:17,497
They probably met in person
at least once, right?

118
00:05:17,623 --> 00:05:18,665
That's a good point.

119
00:05:19,374 --> 00:05:21,460
Can we use Fletcher's personal phone
to track his movements?

120
00:05:21,585 --> 00:05:23,211
{\an8}Definitely...
every location we visit

121
00:05:23,337 --> 00:05:25,380
{\an8}is tracked and time-stamped
on our phones.

122
00:05:25,631 --> 00:05:27,841
I can use the cell tower hits
to track his path.

123
00:05:27,966 --> 00:05:29,301
- How long will it take you?
- 10 minutes.

124
00:05:29,426 --> 00:05:31,595
{\an8}All right. Text the list
of locations to me and Vega.

125
00:05:31,803 --> 00:05:32,971
{\an8}We'll canvass. Let's go.

126
00:05:33,430 --> 00:05:34,473
Okay.

127
00:05:42,397 --> 00:05:45,192
{\an8}Hey. I hear you were getting
locations for Cho.

128
00:05:45,567 --> 00:05:46,818
Yeah, I just sent them.

129
00:05:47,069 --> 00:05:48,111
{\an8}Oh, good.

130
00:05:50,489 --> 00:05:53,533
Can I ask you about something,
outside of work?

131
00:05:53,659 --> 00:05:55,994
W-well, it's...
it's not totally outside of work.

132
00:05:56,119 --> 00:05:57,287
You asked Vega out.

133
00:05:58,789 --> 00:06:01,083
- How did you know?
- Ah, this is not my first rodeo.

134
00:06:01,208 --> 00:06:03,460
- What's your question?
- I'm trying to find a restaurant.

135
00:06:03,669 --> 00:06:04,920
And you wanna know
how expensive.

136
00:06:05,045 --> 00:06:06,171
Well, I don't wanna tip my hand.

137
00:06:06,296 --> 00:06:07,881
I think you already tipped your hand.

138
00:06:08,048 --> 00:06:11,927
{\an8}Okay, but how do I impress her
without coming on too strong?

139
00:06:12,552 --> 00:06:13,679
{\an8}Keep it casual.

140
00:06:14,262 --> 00:06:15,722
{\an8}Not a hole in a wall, you know?

141
00:06:15,931 --> 00:06:18,100
{\an8}Tablecloths, not necessarily white.

142
00:06:19,017 --> 00:06:20,060
{\an8}Okay.

143
00:06:21,728 --> 00:06:22,813
And, Wylie?

144
00:06:23,772 --> 00:06:26,316
She already said yes.
That was the hard part.

145
00:06:26,858 --> 00:06:28,110
{\an8}Just try to have fun.

146
00:06:28,694 --> 00:06:30,028
{\an8}Oh, thanks.

147
00:06:37,911 --> 00:06:40,330
{\an8}Wylie sent the list.
There are...

148
00:06:41,790 --> 00:06:44,001
{\an8}14 locations Fletcher visited.

149
00:06:44,126 --> 00:06:45,210
We can cover those today.

150
00:06:45,836 --> 00:06:46,920
They're all over the county.

151
00:06:47,170 --> 00:06:48,797
{\an8}- We wearing jetpacks?
- We'll get it done.

152
00:06:49,673 --> 00:06:50,966
{\an8}If you say so.

153
00:06:59,266 --> 00:07:01,351
- You're definitely taking over the team?
- Yes.

154
00:07:02,310 --> 00:07:03,478
Are you excited?

155
00:07:04,021 --> 00:07:05,439
I don't really think about it that way.

156
00:07:06,314 --> 00:07:09,026
Isn't this something you've wanted
your entire career?

157
00:07:09,234 --> 00:07:11,611
- Yes.
- So be excited about it.

158
00:07:13,030 --> 00:07:14,072
I am.

159
00:07:14,448 --> 00:07:16,241
Oh. Good.

160
00:07:17,325 --> 00:07:19,995
So, are there any changes
you're going to make

161
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,163
when you take over?

162
00:07:21,413 --> 00:07:22,456
Yeah. A new rule.

163
00:07:22,914 --> 00:07:24,791
Rookie agents are seen
and not heard.

164
00:07:25,042 --> 00:07:26,126
Good luck with that.

165
00:07:34,468 --> 00:07:36,553
Hey. Where have you been?

166
00:07:37,929 --> 00:07:40,891
- For your pillow.
- Oh. Mints. Thank you.

167
00:07:41,475 --> 00:07:45,020
I also got us a reservation
this weekend at the Alhambra.

168
00:07:45,187 --> 00:07:47,230
Resort-ish style place, room service

169
00:07:47,522 --> 00:07:49,733
high-thread-count sheets.
I think you're gonna like it.

170
00:07:49,858 --> 00:07:50,942
You didn't have to do that.

171
00:07:51,068 --> 00:07:53,361
No, I didn't, but I wanna spend
some time alone with you

172
00:07:53,487 --> 00:07:55,155
and it should be at some place
that you like.

173
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:57,616
Well, are you gonna like it?
It doesn't sound very rustic.

174
00:07:57,741 --> 00:07:58,992
Yeah, I'll find a tree.

175
00:07:59,409 --> 00:08:01,161
Uh, this is the security footage.

176
00:08:01,661 --> 00:08:04,331
Yeah, uh, could you, uh,
replay it back from the beginning

177
00:08:04,456 --> 00:08:06,249
- uh, all at the same time?
- Sure.

178
00:08:08,710 --> 00:08:09,753
Stop it.

179
00:08:11,338 --> 00:08:13,882
That's the Alpha.
He's the one in charge.

180
00:08:14,007 --> 00:08:16,802
That's what I thought, too.
He's the only one who touches the money.

181
00:08:17,094 --> 00:08:19,679
Uh, you see that guy over there
with the semi-automatic?

182
00:08:20,097 --> 00:08:21,306
He's the new crew member.

183
00:08:21,765 --> 00:08:25,393
Uh, none of the previous robbery victims
reported heavy weaponry.

184
00:08:25,519 --> 00:08:28,271
- The big gun stands out.
- Good eye.

185
00:08:28,814 --> 00:08:31,900
You notice how the Alpha never turns
his back on him and vice-versa?

186
00:08:32,025 --> 00:08:33,068
They don't trust each other.

187
00:08:33,193 --> 00:08:35,487
The Alpha does turn his back
on the driver.

188
00:08:36,196 --> 00:08:38,740
- What does that mean?
- Well, they're brothers, obviously.

189
00:08:38,907 --> 00:08:39,950
Brothers?

190
00:08:40,075 --> 00:08:41,368
Well, the Alpha has a limp.

191
00:08:41,576 --> 00:08:43,411
It looks like he has a lift
in his left shoe.

192
00:08:44,204 --> 00:08:45,580
That leg must be shorter.

193
00:08:46,081 --> 00:08:48,834
And the driver has a very similar walk.

194
00:08:49,501 --> 00:08:52,212
Different-size legs
is a genetic anomaly.

195
00:08:52,337 --> 00:08:53,380
Brothers.

196
00:08:53,672 --> 00:08:55,048
I'll go tell Cho and Vega.

197
00:08:57,092 --> 00:08:58,802
Did I say you could have
one of those?

198
00:09:07,427 --> 00:09:10,847
Number 4, 10 to go.
Those jetpacks sound better and better.

199
00:09:10,972 --> 00:09:13,391
- Be with you in a minute.
- FBI.

200
00:09:14,017 --> 00:09:15,560
I'm Agent Cho. This is Agent Vega.

201
00:09:16,061 --> 00:09:18,104
Okay. What's this about?

202
00:09:19,272 --> 00:09:20,440
Do you recognize this guy?

203
00:09:21,107 --> 00:09:22,650
He came in for breakfast
on Sunday.

204
00:09:23,818 --> 00:09:24,861
If you say so.

205
00:09:24,986 --> 00:09:26,529
We get a lotta people in here
on the weekends.

206
00:09:26,988 --> 00:09:28,031
Is there something wrong?

207
00:09:28,865 --> 00:09:30,950
I'm busy. I have customers.

208
00:09:32,118 --> 00:09:33,161
Cho.

209
00:09:37,415 --> 00:09:40,835
Lisbon's text said two of the robbers
had trouble with their left leg.

210
00:09:42,712 --> 00:09:44,005
See that table back there?

211
00:09:44,839 --> 00:09:46,966
Look at the boot on that guy's left foot.

212
00:09:50,762 --> 00:09:51,805
This is Cho.

213
00:09:52,097 --> 00:09:54,516
I need backup
at 5219 Burnett Road.

214
00:09:54,641 --> 00:09:56,101
Possible robbery suspects inside.

215
00:10:03,233 --> 00:10:04,275
Hey, guys.

216
00:10:06,319 --> 00:10:09,072
- Is there a problem?
- No problem. I just wanna talk.

217
00:10:09,823 --> 00:10:10,949
Why don't we go outside?

218
00:10:11,366 --> 00:10:12,450
Let's get outta here.

219
00:10:14,786 --> 00:10:16,579
Let me see your hands.
Don't move.

220
00:10:17,122 --> 00:10:18,623
Stay calm, everybody.
Don't panic.

221
00:10:18,748 --> 00:10:21,251
- And where's the third guy?
- What third guy?

222
00:10:29,092 --> 00:10:30,301
I got this one!
Go!

223
00:10:45,358 --> 00:10:47,318
Drop the gun! Down on the ground!
Do it now!

224
00:10:54,909 --> 00:10:57,120
"Tommy! No!"

225
00:10:58,037 --> 00:10:59,330
Go! Go!

226
00:11:04,252 --> 00:11:05,545
"Go! Go!"

227
00:11:13,845 --> 00:11:15,722
Clear out. Get outta the way.

228
00:11:19,058 --> 00:11:20,685
Call 911. Tell them officer down.

229
00:11:21,394 --> 00:11:22,770
- I need to find my phone.
- Come here. Come here.

230
00:11:22,896 --> 00:11:24,814
- Come here.
- I need to call it in, Cho.

231
00:11:24,939 --> 00:11:26,608
No, no, no. They're coming.
They're coming.

232
00:11:26,816 --> 00:11:28,818
Okay, good.
Keep breathing, keep breathing.

233
00:11:28,943 --> 00:11:31,070
Stay with me, okay?
Good. Good.

234
00:11:31,196 --> 00:11:32,447
All right, I just need you to calm down.

235
00:11:32,572 --> 00:11:34,199
Good. All right.
Now, this is gonna hurt, all right?

236
00:11:34,741 --> 00:11:35,992
I know. I know.

237
00:11:36,284 --> 00:11:37,619
I know. You're okay. You're okay.
Keep breathing.

238
00:11:37,744 --> 00:11:39,162
Good, good, good. Keep breathing.

239
00:11:39,329 --> 00:11:40,747
- Where are they?
- Now, they're on their way.

240
00:11:40,872 --> 00:11:42,499
They're on their way, okay?

241
00:11:42,707 --> 00:11:45,793
- It hurts.
- I know. I know. I know.

242
00:11:45,919 --> 00:11:47,837
- Just keep breathing.
- Did I mess up?

243
00:11:47,962 --> 00:11:50,089
No. No, you did good, okay?

244
00:11:50,298 --> 00:11:51,591
- You did good. Yeah, yeah.
- I did?

245
00:11:51,758 --> 00:11:53,051
All right, now just keep breathing
for me.

246
00:11:53,176 --> 00:11:55,220
Okay? Keep breathing.
Good. In, out.

247
00:11:55,678 --> 00:11:56,888
Okay, you're doing good.

248
00:11:57,013 --> 00:11:59,015
Hey. Hey, look at me, Michelle.

249
00:11:59,349 --> 00:12:01,559
Michelle. Hey. Just keep breathing.

250
00:12:01,809 --> 00:12:03,061
Good. Keep breathing.

251
00:12:04,771 --> 00:12:08,191
"Hey. Michelle, look at me.
Look at me, Michelle."

252
00:13:50,174 --> 00:13:51,383
Excuse me.

253
00:13:54,803 --> 00:13:56,430
Is this where Agent Vega worked?

254
00:13:57,222 --> 00:13:59,391
- Sorry?
- I'm Detective Brian Portis.

255
00:13:59,516 --> 00:14:02,603
Austin homicide.
I've been assigned to Agent Vega's case.

256
00:14:03,479 --> 00:14:05,272
- She work here?
- Yes.

257
00:14:07,399 --> 00:14:09,026
I'm very sorry for your loss.

258
00:14:12,196 --> 00:14:13,322
Which was her desk?

259
00:14:15,491 --> 00:14:16,825
I'm gonna have to ask that nobody
touch that

260
00:14:16,951 --> 00:14:18,911
- till I've had a chance to go through it.
- We know.

261
00:14:20,371 --> 00:14:22,039
You know where I can find Agent Abbott?

262
00:14:22,414 --> 00:14:23,958
His office is right around there.

263
00:14:24,875 --> 00:14:26,752
Okay. Thanks.

264
00:14:45,062 --> 00:14:48,524
I'm sorry about this.
Just a B.S. regulation.

265
00:14:48,774 --> 00:14:51,026
You're not allowed to investigate
the death of your own guy.

266
00:14:51,402 --> 00:14:52,486
Yeah, I get it.

267
00:14:52,695 --> 00:14:53,904
We lost a man last year.

268
00:14:55,114 --> 00:14:56,907
Sheriff's department took over.

269
00:14:57,449 --> 00:14:58,492
It's hard.

270
00:14:58,701 --> 00:15:00,703
You wanna be the one to catch
the bastards.

271
00:15:01,996 --> 00:15:04,665
Point is, I know what this is like.

272
00:15:05,416 --> 00:15:07,209
Want you to know
I'm here to work with you.

273
00:15:09,378 --> 00:15:10,421
Okay.

274
00:15:11,588 --> 00:15:13,465
The diner hostess opened right up.

275
00:15:14,008 --> 00:15:15,509
The crew were regulars.

276
00:15:15,718 --> 00:15:18,804
We worked the video surveillance
and ID'd the suspects.

277
00:15:20,305 --> 00:15:23,100
Aaron Brunell. Goes by "Ace".

278
00:15:23,267 --> 00:15:26,061
Seems to be the brains of the operation,
such as they are.

279
00:15:26,854 --> 00:15:31,025
Tommy Brunell, younger brother.
He's the one got shot.

280
00:15:32,026 --> 00:15:36,488
Steve Sellers.
Long sheet, lot of violent felonies.

281
00:15:38,157 --> 00:15:39,658
He's the one that shot your agent.

282
00:15:44,496 --> 00:15:46,540
Apologies, but I have to ask this.

283
00:15:46,790 --> 00:15:48,876
Did Vega do anything unusual
this morning?

284
00:15:49,001 --> 00:15:50,335
Anything different about her?

285
00:15:52,546 --> 00:15:55,549
I don't know. I didn't talk to her.
Not even a "good morning".

286
00:15:55,716 --> 00:15:57,468
It's okay. I'll take that for a "no".

287
00:15:57,885 --> 00:15:59,636
Look, you need to understand something.

288
00:16:00,387 --> 00:16:01,764
You can have the collar.

289
00:16:02,347 --> 00:16:05,350
Your department can take the credit.
I don't give a damn about that.

290
00:16:06,810 --> 00:16:09,104
But this case is ours.

291
00:16:09,438 --> 00:16:12,316
And these men, they belong to us.

292
00:16:14,818 --> 00:16:15,986
Yeah, I get it.

293
00:16:16,570 --> 00:16:17,613
Good.

294
00:16:20,157 --> 00:16:21,950
I'm gonna need to talk to
the agent that was with her.

295
00:16:23,368 --> 00:16:24,411
Okay.

296
00:16:31,710 --> 00:16:34,379
You're Cho, right?
Portis, Austin PD.

297
00:16:34,755 --> 00:16:36,757
If you wanna take some time
to clean up, that's fine.

298
00:16:36,965 --> 00:16:38,008
I'm okay.

299
00:16:38,258 --> 00:16:39,426
Seriously, I can wait.

300
00:16:43,430 --> 00:16:44,473
All right.

301
00:16:51,438 --> 00:16:55,275
Detective Portis interviewing
FBI Special Agent Kimball Cho

302
00:16:55,442 --> 00:16:57,694
regarding the homicide
of Michelle Vega.

303
00:17:01,865 --> 00:17:04,159
Can you walk me through the events
that led up to the shooting?

304
00:17:07,746 --> 00:17:09,790
Vega and I went out canvassing
a little after 10:00.

305
00:17:11,041 --> 00:17:12,334
We were checking locations

306
00:17:12,835 --> 00:17:15,712
where we believed the three suspects
had met up with a co-conspirator.

307
00:17:16,797 --> 00:17:19,591
We'd checked four locations
when we arrived at the diner.

308
00:17:20,425 --> 00:17:22,469
I identified myself to the hostess.

309
00:17:23,929 --> 00:17:26,723
It was at this point that Vega
spotted two of our suspects.

310
00:17:26,849 --> 00:17:28,308
She brought this to my attention.

311
00:17:32,271 --> 00:17:35,149
Hey. How did it go with Portis?

312
00:17:36,024 --> 00:17:37,151
Fine. Seems okay.

313
00:17:37,526 --> 00:17:40,654
Okay.
Look, you know I have to make the call.

314
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:45,325
Vega's file says that her next-of-kin
is an aunt in Tampa.

315
00:17:46,243 --> 00:17:48,745
- Did she ever mention anyone else?
- It's her father's sister.

316
00:17:48,871 --> 00:17:50,789
She's the only living relative
as far as I know.

317
00:17:51,248 --> 00:17:53,000
Okay. All right,
well, I thought I'd just check.

318
00:17:53,125 --> 00:17:54,376
I'll make the call.

319
00:17:54,668 --> 00:17:56,503
- You don't have to.
- Yeah, I do.

320
00:17:57,546 --> 00:17:58,881
I was there. I should do it.

321
00:18:01,341 --> 00:18:03,552
Use my office.
Her number's on the computer.

322
00:19:05,489 --> 00:19:06,657
Ms. Vega?

323
00:19:08,492 --> 00:19:10,911
This is Kimball Cho.
I'm with the FBI in Austin.

324
00:19:13,956 --> 00:19:15,666
Yes, uh, it's about Michelle.

325
00:19:27,219 --> 00:19:28,470
Is there any more coffee?

326
00:19:28,762 --> 00:19:31,139
Uh, actually, I think we're out.
I'll, I'll make some more tea.

327
00:19:31,265 --> 00:19:33,767
No. No, that's okay. I'm fine.

328
00:19:38,855 --> 00:19:41,525
You don't believe
in the afterlife at all, do you?

329
00:19:42,109 --> 00:19:43,151
No.

330
00:19:44,736 --> 00:19:45,779
I do.

331
00:19:48,031 --> 00:19:49,408
Do you think that's foolish?

332
00:19:52,369 --> 00:19:53,662
No, of course not.

333
00:19:55,163 --> 00:19:57,958
I just need to believe
that she's someplace.

334
00:19:58,083 --> 00:19:59,459
Yeah. Yeah.

335
00:20:01,837 --> 00:20:03,755
Austin PD might have
caught something.

336
00:20:12,264 --> 00:20:13,724
A few minutes ago, a gas station attendant

337
00:20:13,849 --> 00:20:16,643
spotted three men in a minivan
matching our description.

338
00:20:16,768 --> 00:20:19,146
They were trying to buy bandages
probably for their wounded guy.

339
00:20:19,396 --> 00:20:20,981
They didn't find what they needed
so they bolted.

340
00:20:21,148 --> 00:20:22,899
- Where?
- Windsor Park.

341
00:20:23,734 --> 00:20:25,569
Couple minutes head start
from the gas station.

342
00:20:25,694 --> 00:20:27,404
They couldn't have gotten
more than a mile or so.

343
00:20:27,612 --> 00:20:29,323
We'll have officers canvassing
the whole area.

344
00:20:29,531 --> 00:20:32,117
- And a K-9 unit.
- And a couple birds in the air.

345
00:20:32,284 --> 00:20:34,453
We might wanna institute
a shelter-in-place order.

346
00:20:34,578 --> 00:20:36,955
Uh, maybe we should all
just take a breath.

347
00:20:37,164 --> 00:20:39,666
We got these guys contained.
We can find them right now.

348
00:20:39,833 --> 00:20:41,626
Well, or they'll see the cops
running around

349
00:20:41,752 --> 00:20:44,463
and the helicopters flying,
and they'll go into hiding.

350
00:20:45,130 --> 00:20:47,591
No, when you're hunting
a wounded animal

351
00:20:47,716 --> 00:20:49,551
you don't just start
chasing it immediately.

352
00:20:49,676 --> 00:20:52,012
- You'll drive it to ground.
- What's the alternative?

353
00:20:53,138 --> 00:20:57,351
Well, no dragnet, no helicopters.
We make 'em feel safe.

354
00:20:57,768 --> 00:20:59,603
Or they'll flee
and then we'll lose 'em.

355
00:20:59,728 --> 00:21:02,606
Well, they're not thinking about fleeing.
They have more basic needs.

356
00:21:03,357 --> 00:21:06,401
They were trying to find medical
supplies for their wounded man.

357
00:21:06,693 --> 00:21:08,070
They can't go to the hospital.

358
00:21:08,487 --> 00:21:10,781
We could put our people outside
local drugstores

359
00:21:10,906 --> 00:21:12,324
let them come to us.

360
00:21:13,408 --> 00:21:15,619
I said I'd work with you.
What do you want?

361
00:21:17,162 --> 00:21:18,622
I say we go with Jane's idea.

362
00:21:18,789 --> 00:21:21,625
All right. How many drugstores
are inside that radius?

363
00:21:22,626 --> 00:21:23,668
A dozen.

364
00:21:23,794 --> 00:21:25,045
We're gonna need some more bodies.

365
00:21:25,504 --> 00:21:26,671
All right. We'll take it.

366
00:21:27,130 --> 00:21:28,840
You stay back and monitor
the radio.

367
00:21:29,091 --> 00:21:30,133
Sure.

368
00:21:36,765 --> 00:21:39,101
It's Caldwell. I'm at location one.

369
00:21:43,188 --> 00:21:44,564
This is Cho, location two.

370
00:21:45,690 --> 00:21:47,442
"Lisbon, location seven."

371
00:21:48,402 --> 00:21:49,861
"Abbott, location ten."

372
00:21:50,320 --> 00:21:51,822
"Swafford, location four."

373
00:21:53,824 --> 00:21:55,742
"Millovich, location 5."

374
00:22:03,542 --> 00:22:05,877
Abbott, location ten.
I have one of 'em.

375
00:22:12,008 --> 00:22:15,220
He just entered a drugstore...
1145 Terrapin.

376
00:22:16,763 --> 00:22:19,266
Everybody move in.
We need eyes on all of them.

377
00:22:19,474 --> 00:22:21,435
And keep it quiet.
No sirens, no lights.

378
00:22:35,866 --> 00:22:38,702
Just left the drugstore,
headed south on Terrapin.

379
00:22:41,705 --> 00:22:43,498
Turn the sirens off!

380
00:22:46,168 --> 00:22:47,419
He knows we're here.

381
00:22:50,547 --> 00:22:52,090
Brunell, drop the gun!

382
00:22:52,924 --> 00:22:55,177
- Let the woman go!
- Go to hell!

383
00:22:57,846 --> 00:22:58,889
Go!

384
00:23:00,265 --> 00:23:01,558
Get in! Get in!

385
00:23:10,984 --> 00:23:12,861
Suspects are traveling
in a gold minivan

386
00:23:12,986 --> 00:23:14,529
with Texas license plates.

387
00:23:14,654 --> 00:23:16,865
"They have a hostage.
Maintain pursuit."

388
00:23:16,990 --> 00:23:20,243
"Do not...
I repeat, do not engage."

389
00:23:48,870 --> 00:23:50,371
- They're inside?
- Yeah.

390
00:23:50,496 --> 00:23:51,873
The uniforms couldn't stop them.

391
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:53,499
Drove right into the garage.

392
00:23:53,750 --> 00:23:55,793
The house belongs to Susan Cofield.

393
00:23:56,169 --> 00:23:57,670
Early 70s, diabetic.

394
00:23:57,795 --> 00:23:59,172
We don't know if they're allowing
her access

395
00:23:59,297 --> 00:24:00,340
to her medications.

396
00:24:00,465 --> 00:24:02,342
She lives with her nephew, Phil.
He's in there, too.

397
00:24:02,467 --> 00:24:04,218
- Has anyone spoken to them?
- Portis just did

398
00:24:04,344 --> 00:24:05,386
but we don't know what they said.

399
00:24:05,511 --> 00:24:07,180
He had to go talk to his superiors first.

400
00:24:12,393 --> 00:24:14,562
We, we have money, jewelry.
We...

401
00:24:14,729 --> 00:24:15,772
Shut up.

402
00:24:17,482 --> 00:24:18,816
It's gonna be okay, buddy.

403
00:24:19,567 --> 00:24:21,110
Okay? Breathe, breathe. Hey.

404
00:24:24,447 --> 00:24:28,034
Sorry. Hey, hey, look at me.
Look at me.

405
00:24:28,368 --> 00:24:31,579
I need you to breathe. Okay?
It's gonna be okay.

406
00:24:39,504 --> 00:24:41,089
Okay. What are they asking for?

407
00:24:41,214 --> 00:24:43,549
Food, a doctor for the wounded guy

408
00:24:43,716 --> 00:24:45,426
a helicopter, and a pilot.

409
00:24:45,551 --> 00:24:48,054
They really are just making it up
as they're going along, aren't they?

410
00:24:48,304 --> 00:24:51,849
Normally we should establish trust
try to humanize the hostages but...

411
00:24:52,225 --> 00:24:53,518
I don't know if that's gonna work.

412
00:24:53,768 --> 00:24:55,687
I don't think these guys
have much compassion.

413
00:24:55,895 --> 00:24:57,063
Well, I wouldn't say that.

414
00:24:57,689 --> 00:24:59,982
It's a question of who
they have compassion for.

415
00:25:00,274 --> 00:25:03,444
- These guys killed Vega.
- Sellers did, not Ace.

416
00:25:04,362 --> 00:25:07,699
They're in there because he was trying
to get medicine for his brother.

417
00:25:08,783 --> 00:25:09,951
That's compassion.

418
00:25:10,660 --> 00:25:11,786
Should we send Tommy a doctor?

419
00:25:11,911 --> 00:25:13,830
Trade that for releasing
one of the hostages?

420
00:25:13,955 --> 00:25:15,331
Well, I was gonna say the opposite.

421
00:25:15,456 --> 00:25:18,751
Ace is desperate. I-if we help him,
then we lose our best leverage.

422
00:25:19,293 --> 00:25:21,421
Our best bet is to just
let Tommy suffer.

423
00:25:21,546 --> 00:25:23,131
Sellers is in this for the money.

424
00:25:23,923 --> 00:25:25,508
I mean, he'd probably
just as well let Tommy die.

425
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:29,220
Well, that's even better.
We drive a wedge between them.

426
00:25:29,429 --> 00:25:30,680
Divide and conquer.

427
00:25:31,222 --> 00:25:33,850
Okay. Let's try it.

428
00:25:34,058 --> 00:25:35,560
Is there anything we can give 'em?

429
00:25:49,866 --> 00:25:52,076
- Try anything, she dies.
- I won't.

430
00:25:52,577 --> 00:25:53,619
Here.

431
00:25:55,329 --> 00:25:56,539
What about a doctor?

432
00:25:57,123 --> 00:25:58,708
My brother's hurt real bad.

433
00:25:59,876 --> 00:26:01,753
- Yeah, you can have a doctor.
- When?

434
00:26:01,878 --> 00:26:03,171
As soon as you surrender.

435
00:26:06,632 --> 00:26:09,552
"Altercation with two Austin FBI agents"

436
00:26:09,677 --> 00:26:11,387
"at the Tastee Pancake House."

437
00:26:11,554 --> 00:26:14,265
- "Shots were fired..."
- What were you talking to the cops about?

438
00:26:14,515 --> 00:26:15,558
Nothing.

439
00:26:17,518 --> 00:26:18,895
We said no secrets.

440
00:26:20,688 --> 00:26:22,023
I asked if we can get a doctor.

441
00:26:22,523 --> 00:26:24,484
They're not gonna give you that
unless you give something up

442
00:26:24,650 --> 00:26:27,361
like one of them, and there is
no way in hell I'm doing that.

443
00:26:27,487 --> 00:26:28,529
He is dying.

444
00:26:28,654 --> 00:26:30,573
Yeah, and it's not my fault
the dude got himself shot.

445
00:26:33,534 --> 00:26:35,870
"I'm not going back to jail
to save his sorry ass."

446
00:26:35,995 --> 00:26:37,580
"We agreed that we were gonna
get some help."

447
00:26:37,705 --> 00:26:40,166
"Yeah, and that's before we had
a million cops on our ass."

448
00:26:41,042 --> 00:26:43,377
Well, looks like it's working.

449
00:26:43,711 --> 00:26:45,630
You wanted division, you got it.

450
00:26:45,797 --> 00:26:48,216
Well, it's a good start,
but we need to stir the pot.

451
00:26:48,883 --> 00:26:50,885
Can you hear a television on in there?

452
00:26:51,636 --> 00:26:53,137
Sounds like the local news.

453
00:26:53,346 --> 00:26:54,847
Probably watching their own coverage.

454
00:26:55,097 --> 00:26:56,140
Excellent.

455
00:27:01,187 --> 00:27:02,230
Can I talk to you?

456
00:27:05,858 --> 00:27:06,943
I got a look inside.

457
00:27:07,276 --> 00:27:09,028
I think if we went in,
we could take them out.

458
00:27:09,237 --> 00:27:11,113
There's three armed men in there.
Things could get ugly.

459
00:27:11,239 --> 00:27:13,324
- What about the hostages?
- I think we can keep them out of it.

460
00:27:13,533 --> 00:27:15,910
And if we don't do something soon
they could get hurt, or worse.

461
00:27:16,077 --> 00:27:17,995
- Jane says he has a plan.
- No.

462
00:27:18,246 --> 00:27:19,372
He's improvising.

463
00:27:19,747 --> 00:27:21,624
Now, I've followed Jane down
a lotta paths

464
00:27:21,749 --> 00:27:22,959
but I'm not sure he's right this time.

465
00:27:23,084 --> 00:27:25,002
You wanna go in
and take these guys out?

466
00:27:25,962 --> 00:27:28,881
Is that about... payback for Vega?

467
00:27:29,382 --> 00:27:30,424
Maybe.

468
00:27:32,593 --> 00:27:33,636
What if it is?

469
00:27:37,557 --> 00:27:39,851
Let's let Jane's plan play out
for a little bit.

470
00:27:39,976 --> 00:27:43,646
In the meantime, talk to SWAT
let 'em know we might wanna go in.

471
00:27:46,649 --> 00:27:47,859
Interesting.

472
00:27:48,234 --> 00:27:50,194
Which of the hostage takers
are you negotiating with?

473
00:27:50,319 --> 00:27:51,445
Sorry. Can't say.

474
00:27:51,654 --> 00:27:52,989
Can I at least quote you
by name, Mr. Jane?

475
00:27:53,114 --> 00:27:56,117
- No, uh, a well-placed source.
- That works.

476
00:28:01,706 --> 00:28:04,166
"Let's go now to our reporter,
Elizabeth Kerrigan"

477
00:28:04,292 --> 00:28:05,334
"who is on the scene."

478
00:28:05,501 --> 00:28:06,711
"Elizabeth, what are you hearing?"

479
00:28:07,044 --> 00:28:10,298
"Thanks, George.
Officially, no deal has been made."

480
00:28:10,423 --> 00:28:12,842
"But a well-placed source
tells me one hostage taker"

481
00:28:12,967 --> 00:28:15,720
"has started back-channel negotiations
for surrender."

482
00:28:16,679 --> 00:28:18,180
What the hell?

483
00:28:18,931 --> 00:28:20,933
You talking to the pigs
behind my back?

484
00:28:21,267 --> 00:28:22,310
Quiet!

485
00:28:27,565 --> 00:28:29,317
I don't know
what that bitch is talking about.

486
00:28:30,943 --> 00:28:33,404
Trying to cut your own deal,
sell me out?

487
00:28:33,529 --> 00:28:34,572
No.

488
00:28:34,697 --> 00:28:36,532
Please let us go. Please.

489
00:28:41,787 --> 00:28:43,331
You got something to say?

490
00:28:44,373 --> 00:28:45,416
Please!

491
00:28:46,417 --> 00:28:47,460
Sit down.

492
00:28:48,502 --> 00:28:49,712
That's what I thought.

493
00:29:10,358 --> 00:29:12,068
All right, four teams will cover
the perimeter of the house.

494
00:29:12,193 --> 00:29:13,653
Alpha team will make initial entry.

495
00:29:13,819 --> 00:29:15,988
- What are you doing?
- The situation is escalating.

496
00:29:16,113 --> 00:29:17,573
One of the hostages was attacked.

497
00:29:17,698 --> 00:29:19,450
We think he's okay,
but that may not last.

498
00:29:19,659 --> 00:29:21,661
We're afraid that someone
is gonna get seriously hurt, Jane.

499
00:29:21,786 --> 00:29:22,912
Just give me a little more time.

500
00:29:23,079 --> 00:29:24,830
I'm sorry, Jane. We tried.

501
00:29:25,331 --> 00:29:26,707
- We move in five.
- All right.

502
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:30,086
- Don't go with them.
- We know what we're doing.

503
00:29:30,628 --> 00:29:32,964
- Look, you don't have to.
- Yes, I do.

504
00:29:33,214 --> 00:29:34,966
Abbott and Cho, they don't wanna make
an arrest.

505
00:29:35,091 --> 00:29:36,676
They wanna kill these guys.

506
00:29:36,926 --> 00:29:40,054
- Other people might get hurt.
- It is not gonna go down like that.

507
00:29:40,179 --> 00:29:41,973
- We'll be all right.
- Y-you don't know that.

508
00:29:42,932 --> 00:29:44,558
- Lisbon.
- I have to go.

509
00:29:50,231 --> 00:29:51,857
All right, you two sweep left,
you two stay center.

510
00:29:51,983 --> 00:29:53,776
- Lisbon, you're with me.
- What the hell's your guy doing?

511
00:29:54,068 --> 00:29:55,653
Who? Jane!

512
00:29:56,278 --> 00:29:57,613
- Hey!
- Jane!

513
00:29:57,780 --> 00:29:59,657
- Hey, Jane!
- Don't go in there!

514
00:29:59,949 --> 00:30:01,617
- Jane!
- Get back over here!

515
00:30:06,747 --> 00:30:07,790
I'm not armed.

516
00:30:09,667 --> 00:30:10,793
Who are you?

517
00:30:11,627 --> 00:30:14,005
- I can help you and your brother.
- How?

518
00:30:15,089 --> 00:30:18,259
You have to release
a hostage first.

519
00:30:20,845 --> 00:30:23,764
- Forget it.
- I-I-I'm FBI. Take me instead.

520
00:30:24,140 --> 00:30:25,182
What the hell is he doing?

521
00:30:25,307 --> 00:30:26,976
More valuable, better leverage.

522
00:30:30,354 --> 00:30:32,314
What's stopping me
from keeping all three of you?

523
00:30:32,440 --> 00:30:33,941
There's too many people
to watch.

524
00:30:34,316 --> 00:30:35,735
Come on. It's a good deal.

525
00:30:38,821 --> 00:30:39,864
Sellers!

526
00:30:41,615 --> 00:30:42,742
Bring the crier.

527
00:30:45,411 --> 00:30:47,329
- Keep your hands up.
- Oh, yeah.

528
00:30:48,456 --> 00:30:49,665
Don't be stupid.

529
00:30:49,790 --> 00:30:50,833
What is it now?

530
00:30:50,958 --> 00:30:52,877
This guy wants to trade
for that one.

531
00:30:57,757 --> 00:30:59,091
Yeah, whatever.

532
00:31:03,846 --> 00:31:04,930
Okay.

533
00:31:06,474 --> 00:31:07,641
Okay.

534
00:31:20,977 --> 00:31:22,771
I don't understand.
We were about to go in.

535
00:31:22,937 --> 00:31:25,774
I am just as angry as you are,
but he's already in there.

536
00:31:25,899 --> 00:31:27,025
We might as well give him
some time.

537
00:31:27,150 --> 00:31:28,193
Time to do what?

538
00:31:28,318 --> 00:31:30,278
He's trying to drive a wedge
between these two guys

539
00:31:30,403 --> 00:31:31,905
make them turn on each other.

540
00:31:32,071 --> 00:31:34,240
Look, if anybody can do that,
Jane can.

541
00:31:36,159 --> 00:31:37,243
Okay.

542
00:31:37,577 --> 00:31:39,996
Let's take a pause for a bit.
Half-hour.

543
00:31:40,371 --> 00:31:41,414
All right.

544
00:31:42,207 --> 00:31:43,917
"Honestly, I just...
all of a sudden"

545
00:31:44,042 --> 00:31:47,128
"it was all of the SWAT vans
that came outta nowhere"

546
00:31:47,253 --> 00:31:49,714
"and, and this is such
a-a quiet neighborhood."

547
00:31:49,839 --> 00:31:52,008
"You know, we just...
none of us were expecting this."

548
00:31:52,133 --> 00:31:53,301
He's clear.

549
00:31:55,720 --> 00:31:56,888
You stay there.

550
00:31:57,180 --> 00:31:59,557
We need to get in touch with the cops
get them to move on that chopper.

551
00:31:59,891 --> 00:32:01,726
- How the hell we supposed to do that?
- I don't know.

552
00:32:01,935 --> 00:32:04,771
Hey! You do not move
unless I tell you to move.

553
00:32:06,105 --> 00:32:07,607
I just need to make sure
she's okay.

554
00:32:07,774 --> 00:32:08,817
She's okay.

555
00:32:09,526 --> 00:32:10,693
You see that bracelet?

556
00:32:12,403 --> 00:32:14,531
She's diabetic.
She could go into shock.

557
00:32:19,744 --> 00:32:20,787
Okay.

558
00:32:21,663 --> 00:32:22,914
- Okay.
- Thank you.

559
00:32:26,751 --> 00:32:27,794
How you feeling?

560
00:32:28,753 --> 00:32:31,297
Scared, but okay basically.

561
00:32:31,881 --> 00:32:33,716
You sure? You look a little flush.

562
00:32:35,677 --> 00:32:37,846
Feeling, uh, any numbness?

563
00:32:40,557 --> 00:32:43,059
- I-I'm not sure.
- How about your feet?

564
00:32:43,309 --> 00:32:45,520
Y-you feeling numbness
in your feet?

565
00:32:46,271 --> 00:32:47,522
Maybe a little.

566
00:32:49,148 --> 00:32:50,191
That's what I thought.

567
00:32:50,316 --> 00:32:51,943
I'm worried you're gonna start
experiencing loss of vision.

568
00:32:52,402 --> 00:32:54,445
Your...
your breath is getting shorter.

569
00:32:54,654 --> 00:32:56,239
- Oh, God.
- It's okay.

570
00:32:58,241 --> 00:33:00,159
Oh. Oh, God.

571
00:33:00,410 --> 00:33:01,995
- Stay calm.
- Oh, my God.

572
00:33:02,203 --> 00:33:05,373
You got some trouble here.
She's about to go into a diabetic coma.

573
00:33:05,832 --> 00:33:07,667
- Look, it's not my problem.
- Don't be stupid.

574
00:33:07,792 --> 00:33:09,210
They have microphones in here.

575
00:33:09,377 --> 00:33:10,545
They...
they have what? Where?

576
00:33:10,753 --> 00:33:14,173
Everywhere. They can hear
every word we're saying.

577
00:33:14,507 --> 00:33:16,676
If they think she's in danger
they're gonna come right in.

578
00:33:16,801 --> 00:33:18,219
Damn it, I knew it!

579
00:33:18,511 --> 00:33:20,221
Calm down, okay?

580
00:33:20,430 --> 00:33:22,849
Okay, j-j-just hold on a second here.

581
00:33:24,392 --> 00:33:27,020
Okay.
Look, here's what we're gonna do.

582
00:33:27,604 --> 00:33:28,646
You're gonna watch him

583
00:33:29,314 --> 00:33:30,899
I'm gonna take her out
the side gate.

584
00:33:32,567 --> 00:33:33,651
Come on. Let's go.

585
00:33:34,235 --> 00:33:36,487
Just calm down.
I'm gonna take you outta here.

586
00:33:37,906 --> 00:33:38,990
Son of a...

587
00:33:44,329 --> 00:33:45,538
Such a shame.

588
00:33:46,915 --> 00:33:49,125
All this trouble for $800,000.

589
00:33:52,253 --> 00:33:53,838
What do you mean, 800?

590
00:33:54,130 --> 00:33:57,175
That's how much was taken. We got
the official count just a little while ago.

591
00:33:57,300 --> 00:33:58,968
It's 600,
you don't know nothing!

592
00:34:00,178 --> 00:34:02,388
- This is not my business.
- Yeah, you're damn straight!

593
00:34:05,224 --> 00:34:06,476
"You got an official count?"

594
00:34:07,852 --> 00:34:10,897
"I don't wanna take sides
but there was 800 grand on that truck."

595
00:34:12,065 --> 00:34:13,149
"You guys took it all."

596
00:34:13,274 --> 00:34:15,902
That's his plan, the money.
That's a wedge.

597
00:34:16,277 --> 00:34:17,320
"You're full of it."

598
00:34:17,445 --> 00:34:19,113
Doesn't sound like Sellers
believes him.

599
00:34:19,405 --> 00:34:21,366
Then let's give him a reason
to believe.

600
00:34:22,742 --> 00:34:25,161
"And we hear Elizabeth Kerrigan
has some additional details"

601
00:34:25,286 --> 00:34:27,121
"about this morning's
armored-truck robbery."

602
00:34:27,246 --> 00:34:29,165
- "Elizabeth?"
- "Indeed, Eric."

603
00:34:29,415 --> 00:34:30,458
Hey, turn that up.

604
00:34:33,044 --> 00:34:35,755
"We've learned it was
just over $800,000"

605
00:34:35,880 --> 00:34:38,091
"stolen from the Gibbs Security
truck this morning."

606
00:34:38,341 --> 00:34:39,801
"That official count from the bank"

607
00:34:39,926 --> 00:34:42,553
"makes this one of the biggest
robberies in recent history."

608
00:34:43,137 --> 00:34:45,056
These people need to get
their facts straight.

609
00:34:48,309 --> 00:34:49,352
What?

610
00:34:52,271 --> 00:34:53,314
Nothing.

611
00:34:53,898 --> 00:34:55,233
I'm going to take a whiz.

612
00:34:56,234 --> 00:34:57,402
Well, make it quick.

613
00:35:05,493 --> 00:35:07,578
Did he say something to you
when I was outside?

614
00:35:08,579 --> 00:35:10,081
No, n-not...
not much.

615
00:35:10,206 --> 00:35:12,917
He just kept going on about
how he didn't wanna die in prison.

616
00:35:13,418 --> 00:35:14,794
Son of a bitch. Come here.

617
00:35:20,883 --> 00:35:22,135
Get away from the money!

618
00:35:23,261 --> 00:35:25,304
I always knew you were gonna
stab me in the back.

619
00:35:25,513 --> 00:35:27,974
Me? You're the one who screwed me.

620
00:35:28,641 --> 00:35:30,560
- Where did you stash it?
- What stash?

621
00:35:30,893 --> 00:35:32,145
The extra 200 grand.

622
00:35:33,062 --> 00:35:35,148
- You better tell me where it is.
- Screw you!

623
00:36:20,735 --> 00:36:23,821
"One of these days,
the sky's gonna break"

624
00:36:23,946 --> 00:36:26,324
"And everything will escape"

625
00:36:26,449 --> 00:36:29,368
"And I'll know"

626
00:36:33,498 --> 00:36:34,665
"One of these days"

627
00:36:34,791 --> 00:36:38,878
"The mountains are gonna
fall into the sea"

628
00:36:39,212 --> 00:36:41,506
"And they'll know"

629
00:36:46,219 --> 00:36:49,388
"That you and I were made for this"

630
00:36:49,514 --> 00:36:52,683
"I was made to taste your kiss"

631
00:36:52,809 --> 00:37:00,817
"We were made
to never fall away"

632
00:37:05,488 --> 00:37:08,866
"Never fall away"

633
00:37:19,877 --> 00:37:25,341
"One of these days, letters
are gonna fall from the sky"

634
00:37:25,591 --> 00:37:31,264
"Telling us all to go free"

635
00:37:32,306 --> 00:37:35,685
"But until that day, I'll find a way"

636
00:37:35,810 --> 00:37:40,439
"To let everybody know
that you're coming back"

637
00:37:41,065 --> 00:37:44,277
"You're coming back for me"

638
00:37:45,486 --> 00:37:48,531
"'Cause even though
you left me here"

639
00:37:48,656 --> 00:37:51,659
"I have nothing left to fear"

640
00:37:51,909 --> 00:37:55,121
"These are only walls that hold me"

641
00:37:55,246 --> 00:37:59,834
"Here"

642
00:38:05,423 --> 00:38:10,219
"Hold me here"

643
00:38:18,644 --> 00:38:22,940
"Hold me here"

644
00:38:24,609 --> 00:38:28,112
"Hold me here"

645
00:38:29,989 --> 00:38:35,828
"Only walls that hold me here"

646
00:38:44,795 --> 00:38:49,133
"One day soon"

647
00:38:49,342 --> 00:38:52,386
"I'll hold you like the sun"

648
00:38:52,637 --> 00:38:55,348
"Holds the moon"

649
00:38:55,723 --> 00:38:58,893
"And we will hear those planes"

650
00:38:59,101 --> 00:39:01,938
"Overhead"

651
00:39:02,104 --> 00:39:07,652
"And we won't have to be scared"

652
00:39:09,278 --> 00:39:11,822
"Coming back"

653
00:39:12,615 --> 00:39:13,866
How you doin'?

654
00:39:17,245 --> 00:39:19,455
Places like this must be hard
for you.

655
00:39:21,707 --> 00:39:24,627
Anyway, I don't feel like going
this weekend.

656
00:39:24,752 --> 00:39:26,379
It just doesn't seem right.

657
00:39:27,463 --> 00:39:29,090
- Is that okay?
- Yeah.

658
00:39:34,011 --> 00:39:35,721
I can't do this anymore.

659
00:39:37,056 --> 00:39:38,140
What do you mean?

660
00:39:38,307 --> 00:39:40,935
I can't watch you do this work.
I mean, it...

661
00:39:42,186 --> 00:39:43,980
It could've been you in that coffin.

662
00:39:47,858 --> 00:39:49,277
And I don't...

663
00:39:50,569 --> 00:39:52,405
I can't go through that again.

664
00:39:53,990 --> 00:39:55,032
Jane.

665
00:39:55,574 --> 00:39:57,451
You're the one that walked in
that house.

666
00:39:57,576 --> 00:39:59,370
Yes, so that you wouldn't.

667
00:40:00,621 --> 00:40:02,999
You could've died.
How is that different?

668
00:40:03,124 --> 00:40:05,084
Me dying, it's-it's...

669
00:40:05,668 --> 00:40:07,169
It doesn't hurt me.

670
00:40:10,923 --> 00:40:14,343
You can't keep pulling me
from the path of oncoming trains.

671
00:40:14,552 --> 00:40:15,678
Yeah? Why not?

672
00:40:16,137 --> 00:40:19,307
Because there's always
new trains coming every day.

673
00:40:25,438 --> 00:40:26,605
I'm leaving.

674
00:40:28,607 --> 00:40:31,944
Now, you can come with me,
or you can stay here, but...

675
00:40:33,404 --> 00:40:34,530
I have to go.

676
00:40:36,407 --> 00:40:37,533
Where you going?

677
00:40:39,869 --> 00:40:41,245
Someplace nice.
